('practice:chemistry:p1:q1921:en:v1','chemistry',1921,'Atomic structure','Charge of a neutron',
 'answer_explanation','en','iclub_practice_ai_chemistry_p1_atomic_structure_precise_v1_2026_09_25','Charge of a neutron','A neutron has zero electric charge. Protons are positively charged and electrons are negatively charged, while neutrons are electrically neutral. Neutrons still contribute substantially to the mass of the nucleus.',
