 'answer_explanation','en','iclub_practice_ai_chemistry_p1_atomic_structure_precise_v1_2026_09_25','Periodic table position and atomic number','An element is defined by its atomic number, which is the number of protons in its nucleus. The modern Periodic Table is arranged by increasing atomic number. Changing the neutron number makes an isotope, not a different element.',
