('practice:chemistry:p1:q1933:en:v1','chemistry',1933,'Atomic structure','Mass number',
 'answer_explanation','en','iclub_practice_ai_chemistry_p1_atomic_structure_precise_v1_2026_09_25','Mass number','Mass number A is the total number of nucleons in the nucleus: protons plus neutrons. Atomic number Z is only the number of protons. Electrons are not included in mass number.',
