('practice:chemistry:p1:q1954:en:v1','chemistry',1954,'Atomic structure','Neutrons in copper isotope',
 'answer_explanation','en','iclub_practice_ai_chemistry_p1_atomic_structure_precise_v1_2026_09_25','Neutrons in an isotope','For an isotope, mass number A equals protons plus neutrons and atomic number Z equals protons. Therefore the number of neutrons is A - Z. For copper-63 with Z = 29, neutrons = 63 - 29 = 34.',
 'approved','original_iclub',true,encode(digest(convert_to('For an isotope, mass number A equals protons plus neutrons and atomic number Z equals protons. Therefore the number of neutrons is A - Z. For copper-63 with Z = 29, neutrons = 63 - 29 = 34.','UTF8'),'sha256'),'hex'),now(),now()),
('practice:chemistry:p1:q1954:ru:v1','chemistry',1954,'Atomic structure','Neutrons in copper isotope',
 'answer_explanation','ru','iclub_practice_ai_chemistry_p1_atomic_structure_precise_v1_2026_09_25','Число нейтронов в изотопе','Для изотопа массовое число A равно сумме протонов и нейтронов, а атомный номер Z равен числу протонов. Поэтому число нейтронов равно A - Z. Для меди-63 при Z = 29: 63 - 29 = 34 нейтрона.',
