('practice:chemistry:p1:q3041:en:v1','chemistry',3041,'Atomic structure','Rutherford scattering and the nucleus',
 'answer_explanation','en','iclub_practice_ai_chemistry_p1_atomic_structure_precise_v1_2026_09_25','Rutherford scattering and the nucleus','In the alpha-scattering experiment, most alpha particles passed through the foil, showing that atoms are mostly empty space. A very small fraction were deflected through large angles, which showed that positive charge and almost all atomic mass are concentrated in a tiny, dense nucleus.',
